From 446bad8e8c785a43308161994c1641d41e155075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: nexell: add S5P6818 display/HDMI bring-up driver (phase
 1)

First step of HDMI support for the Nexell S5P6818. Mainline has no Nexell
display driver; this adds a minimal platform driver under a new
drivers/gpu/drm/nexell/ that does the hardware-proven foundation: the HDMI
block is clock-gated out of reset (its resets are already released by the
boot chain), so probe() ungates the two DISPLAYTOP clkgen modules feeding
HDMI and then reads the HDMI hotplug (HPD) state.

HW-verified on a NanoPi Fire3 with a monitor attached:
  nexell-display c0100000.display: S5P6818 display: HDMI clocks enabled;
  HPD_STATUS=0x00000001 HPD=0x00000001 -> monitor CONNECTED

DT: a 'nexell,s5p6818-display' node in s5p6818.dtsi (disabled), enabled in
s5p6818-nanopi3-common.dtsi since every board in the family has HDMI.
Kconfig CONFIG_DRM_NEXELL is a bool for now (plain platform driver); it
becomes tristate + depends on DRM when the DPC/HDMI/plane modeset path and
the atomic-KMS glue land. Config symbol added to linux-s5p6818-edge.config
separately.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
